  <subsection title="Multiply Rational Expressions">
    <p>To multiply rational expressions, we do just what we did with numerical fractions. We multiply the numerators and multiply the denominators. Then, if there are any common factors, we remove them to simplify the result.</p>
    <note type="Multiplication of Rational Expressions">
      <p>If $$p,q,r,s$$ are polynomials where $$q \neq 0\ \text{and}\ s \neq 0$$, then</p>
      <equation>$$\frac{p}{q} \cdot \frac{r}{s} = \frac{pr}{qs}$$</equation>
      <p>To multiply rational expressions, multiply the numerators and multiply the denominators.</p>
    </note>
    <p>We’ll do the first example with numerical fractions to remind us of how we multiplied fractions without variables.</p>
    <example number="8.17">
      <problem>
        <p>Multiply: $$\frac{10}{28} \cdot \frac{8}{15}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply the numerators and denominators.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Look for common factors, and then remove them.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.33">
      <p>Mulitply: $$\frac{6}{10} \cdot \frac{15}{12}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.34">
      <p>Mulitply: $$\frac{20}{15} \cdot \frac{6}{8}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <p>Remember, throughout this chapter, we will assume that all numerical values that would make the denominator be zero are excluded. We will not write the restrictions for each rational expression, but keep in mind that the denominator can never be zero. So in this next example, $$x \neq 0$$ and $$y \neq 0$$.</p>
    <example number="8.18">
      <problem>
        <p>Mulitply: $$\frac{2x}{3y^{2}} \cdot \frac{6xy^{3}}{x^{2}y}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the numerator and denominator completely, and then remove common factors.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.35">
      <p>Mulitply: $$\frac{3pq}{q^{2}} \cdot \frac{5p^{2}q}{6pq}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.36">
      <p>Mulitply: $$\frac{6x^{3}y}{7x^{2}} \cdot \frac{2xy^{3}}{x^{2}y}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <example number="8.19">
      <problem>
        <p>Mulitply: $$\frac{2x}{x^{2} - 7x + 12} \cdot \frac{x^{2} - 9}{6x^{2}}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution />
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.37">
      <p>Mulitply: $$\frac{5x}{x^{2} + 5x + 6} \cdot \frac{x^{2} - 4}{10x}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.38">
      <p>Mulitply: $$\frac{9x^{2}}{x^{2} + 11x + 30} \cdot \frac{x^{2} - 36}{3x^{2}}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="How To">
      <list type="ol" style="1">
        <item>Step 1. 
Factor each numerator and denominator completely.</item>
        <item>Step 2. 
Multiply the numerators and denominators.</item>
        <item>Step 3. 
Simplify by dividing out common factors.</item>
      </list>
    </note>
    <example number="8.20">
      <problem>
        <p>Multiply: $$\frac{n^{2} - 7n}{n^{2} + 2n + 1} \cdot \frac{n + 1}{2n}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="Step-by-step simplification of a rational algebraic expression.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\frac{n^{2} - 7n}{n^{2} + 2n + 1} \cdot \frac{n + 1}{2n}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor each numerator and denominator.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{n\left( {n - 7} \right)}{\left( {n + 1} \right)\left( {n + 1} \right)} \cdot \frac{n + 1}{2n}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply the numerators and the denominators.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{n\left( {n - 7} \right)\left( {n + 1} \right)}{\left( {n + 1} \right)\left( {n + 1} \right)2n}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Remove common factors.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{n\left( {n - 7} \right)\left( {n + 1} \right)}{\left( {n + 1} \right)\left( {n + 1} \right)2n}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{n - 7}{2\left( {n + 1} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.39">
      <p>Multiply: $$\frac{x^{2} - 25}{x^{2} - 3x - 10} \cdot \frac{x + 2}{x}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.40">
      <p>Multiply: $$\frac{x^{2} - 4x}{x^{2} + 5x + 6} \cdot \frac{x + 2}{x}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <example number="8.21">
      <problem>
        <p>Multiply: $$\frac{16 - 4x}{2x - 12} \cdot \frac{x^{2} - 5x - 6}{x^{2} - 16}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="This table illustrates the step-by-step simplification of a rational algebraic expression through factoring and canceling common terms.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\frac{16 - 4x}{2x - 12} \cdot \frac{x^{2} - 5x - 6}{x^{2} - 16}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor each numerator and denominator.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{4\left( {4 - x} \right)}{2\left( {x - 6} \right)} \cdot \frac{\left( {x - 6} \right)\left( {x + 1} \right)}{\left( {x - 4} \right)\left( {x + 4} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply the numerators and the denominators.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{4\left( {4 - x} \right)\left( {x - 6} \right)\left( {x + 1} \right)}{2\left( {x - 6} \right)\left( {x - 4} \right)\left( {x + 4} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Remove common factors.</cell>
              <cell>$$(-1)\frac{2 \cdot 2\left( {4 - x} \right)\left( {x - 6} \right)\left( {x + 1} \right)}{2\left( {x - 6} \right)\left( {x - 4} \right)\left( {x + 4} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$- \frac{2\left( {x + 1} \right)}{\left( {x + 4} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.41">
      <p>Multiply: $$\frac{12x - 6x^{2}}{x^{2} + 8x} \cdot \frac{x^{2} + 11x + 24}{x^{2} - 4}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.42">
      <p>Multiply: $$\frac{9v - 3v^{2}}{9v + 36} \cdot \frac{v^{2} + 7v + 12}{v^{2} - 9}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <example number="8.22">
      <problem>
        <p>Multiply: $$\frac{2x - 6}{x^{2} - 8x + 15} \cdot \frac{x^{2} - 25}{2x + 10}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor each numerator and denominator.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply the numerators and denominators.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Remove common factors.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.43">
      <p>Multiply: $$\frac{3a - 21}{a^{2} - 9a + 14} \cdot \frac{a^{2} - 4}{3a + 6}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.44">
      <p>Multiply: $$\frac{b^{2} - b}{b^{2} + 9b - 10} \cdot \frac{b^{2} - 100}{b^{2} - 10b}.$$</p>
    </note>
  </subsection>
  <subsection title="Divide Rational Expressions">
    <p>To divide rational expressions we multiply the first fraction by the reciprocal of the second, just like we did for numerical fractions.</p>
    <p>Remember, the reciprocal of $$\frac{a}{b}$$ is $$\frac{b}{a}$$. To find the reciprocal we simply put the numerator in the denominator and the denominator in the numerator. We “flip” the fraction.</p>
    <note type="Division of Rational Expressions">
      <p>If $$p,q,r,s$$ are polynomials where $$q \neq 0,r \neq 0,s \neq 0$$, then</p>
      <equation>$$\frac{p}{q} \div \frac{r}{s} = \frac{p}{q} \cdot \frac{s}{r}$$</equation>
      <p>To divide rational expressions multiply the first fraction by the reciprocal of the second.</p>
    </note>
    <example number="8.23">
      <problem>
        <p>Divide: $$\frac{x + 9}{6 - x} \div \frac{x^{2} - 81}{x - 6}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution />
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.45">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{c + 3}{5 - c} \div \frac{c^{2} - 9}{c - 5}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.46">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{2 - d}{d - 4} \div \frac{4 - d^{2}}{4 - d}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="How To">
      <list type="ol" style="1">
        <item>Step 1. 
Rewrite the division as the product of the first rational expression and the reciprocal of the second.</item>
        <item>Step 2. 
Factor the numerators and denominators completely.</item>
        <item>Step 3. 
Multiply the numerators and denominators together.</item>
        <item>Step 4. 
Simplify by dividing out common factors.</item>
      </list>
    </note>
    <example number="8.24">
      <problem>
        <p>Divide: $$\frac{3n^{2}}{n^{2} - 4n} \div \frac{9n^{2} - 45n}{n^{2} - 7n + 10}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite the division as the product of the first rational
expression and the reciprocal of the second.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the numerators and denominators
and then multiply.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify by dividing out common factors.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.47">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{2m^{2}}{m^{2} - 8m} \div \frac{8m^{2} + 24m}{m^{2} + m - 6}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.48">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{15n^{2}}{3n^{2} + 33n} \div \frac{5n - 5}{n^{2} + 9n - 22}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <p>Remember, first rewrite the division as multiplication of the first expression by the reciprocal of the second. Then factor everything and look for common factors.</p>
    <example number="8.25">
      <problem>
        <p>Divide: $$\frac{2x^{2} + 5x - 12}{x^{2} - 16} \div \frac{2x^{2} - 13x + 15}{x^{2} - 8x + 16}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="Step-by-step simplification of the division of two rational expressions through factoring and canceling common terms.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\frac{2x^{2} + 5x - 12}{x^{2} - 16} \div \frac{2x^{2} - 13x + 15}{x^{2} - 8x + 16}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite the division as multiplication ofthe first expression by the reciprocal of the second.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{2x^{2} + 5x - 12}{x^{2} - 16} \cdot \frac{x^{2} - 8x + 16}{2x^{2} - 13x + 15}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the numerators and denominators and then multiply.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{\left( {2x - 3} \right)\left( {x + 4} \right)\left( {x - 4} \right)\left( {x - 4} \right)}{\left( {x - 4} \right)\left( {x + 4} \right)\left( {2x - 3} \right)\left( {x - 5} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify by dividing out common factors.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{\left( {2x - 3} \right)\left( {x + 4} \right)\left( {x - 4} \right)\left( {x - 4} \right)}{\left( {x - 4} \right)\left( {x + 4} \right)\left( {2x - 3} \right)\left( {x - 5} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{x - 4}{x - 5}$$</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.49">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{3a^{2} - 8a - 3}{a^{2} - 25} \div \frac{3a^{2} - 14a - 5}{a^{2} + 10a + 25}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.50">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{4b^{2} + 7b - 2}{1 - b^{2}} \div \frac{4b^{2} + 15b - 4}{b^{2} - 2b + 1}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <example number="8.26">
      <problem>
        <p>Divide: $$\frac{p^{3} + q^{3}}{2p^{2} + 2pq + 2q^{2}} \div \frac{p^{2} - q^{2}}{6}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="Detailed steps for simplifying a rational algebraic expression through division, multiplication, factoring, and canceling common terms.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\frac{p^{3} + q^{3}}{2p^{2} + 2pq + 2q^{2}} \div \frac{p^{2} - q^{2}}{6}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite the division as a multiplicationof the first expression times thereciprocal of the second.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{p^{3} + q^{3}}{2p^{2} + 2pq + 2q^{2}} \cdot \frac{6}{p^{2} - q^{2}}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the numerators and denominators and then multiply.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{\left( {p + q} \right)\left( {p^{2} - pq + q^{2}} \right)6}{2\left( {p^{2} + pq + q^{2}} \right)\left( {p - q} \right)\left( {p + q} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify by dividing out common factors.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{\left( {p + q} \right)\left( {p^{2} - pq + q^{2}} \right)6^{3}}{2\left( {p^{2} + pq + q^{2}} \right)\left( {p - q} \right)\left( {p + q} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{3\left( {p^{2} - pq + q^{2}} \right)}{\left( {p - q} \right)\left( {p^{2} + pq + q^{2}} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.51">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{x^{3} - 8}{3x^{2} - 6x + 12} \div \frac{x^{2} - 4}{6}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.52">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{2z^{2}}{z^{2} - 1} \div \frac{z^{3} - z^{2} + z}{z^{3} - 1}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <p>Before doing the next example, let’s look at how we divide a fraction by a whole number. When we divide $$\frac{3}{5} \div 4$$, we first write 4 as a fraction so that we can find its reciprocal.</p>
    <equation>$$\begin{array}{l} {\frac{3}{5} \div 4} \\ {\frac{3}{5} \div \frac{4}{1}} \\ {\frac{3}{5} \cdot \frac{1}{4}} \end{array}$$</equation>
    <p>We do the same thing when we divide rational expressions.</p>
    <example number="8.27">
      <problem>
        <p>Divide: $$\frac{a^{2} - b^{2}}{3ab} \div \left( {a^{2} + 2ab + b^{2}} \right).$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="Step-by-step simplification of an algebraic rational expression using division, factoring, and common factor cancellation.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\frac{a^{2} - b^{2}}{3ab} \div \left( {a^{2} + 2ab + b^{2}} \right)$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Write the second expression as a fraction.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{a^{2} - b^{2}}{3ab} \div \frac{a^{2} + 2ab + b^{2}}{1}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite the division as the firstexpression times the reciprocal of thesecond expression.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{a^{2} - b^{2}}{3ab} \cdot \frac{1}{a^{2} + 2ab + b^{2}}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the numerators and thedenominators, and then multiply.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{\left( {a - b} \right)\left( {a + b} \right) \cdot 1}{3ab \cdot \left( {a + b} \right)\left( {a + b} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify by dividing out common factors.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{\left( {a - b} \right)\left( {a + b} \right)}{3ab \cdot \left( {a + b} \right)\left( {a + b} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{\left( {a - b} \right)}{3ab\left( {a + b} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.53">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{2x^{2} - 14x - 16}{4} \div (x^{2} + 2x + 1).$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.54">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{y^{2} - 6y + 8}{y^{2} - 4y} \div (3y^{2} - 12y).$$</p>
    </note>
    <p>Remember a fraction bar means division. A complex fraction is another way of writing division of two fractions.</p>
    <example number="8.28">
      <problem>
        <p>Divide: $$\frac{\frac{6x^{2} - 7x + 2}{4x - 8}}{\frac{2x^{2} - 7x + 3}{x^{2} - 5x + 6}}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="Step-by-step simplification of a complex rational algebraic expression, detailing the process from initial division to the final simplified fraction.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\frac{\frac{6x^{2} - 7x + 2}{4x - 8}}{\frac{2x^{2} - 7x + 3}{x^{2} - 5x + 6}}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite with a division sign.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{6x^{2} - 7x + 2}{4x - 8} \div \frac{2x^{2} - 7x + 3}{x^{2} - 5x + 6}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite as product of first timesreciprocal of second.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{6x^{2} - 7x + 2}{4x - 8} \cdot \frac{x^{2} - 5x + 6}{2x^{2} - 7x + 3}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the numerators and thedenominators, and then multiply.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{\left( {2x - 1} \right)\left( {3x - 2} \right)\left( {x - 2} \right)\left( {x - 3} \right)}{4\left( {x - 2} \right)\left( {2x - 1} \right)\left( {x - 3} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify by dividing out common factors.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{\left( {2x - 1} \right)\left( {3x - 2} \right)\left( {x - 2} \right)\left( {x - 3} \right)}{4\left( {x - 2} \right)\left( {2x - 1} \right)\left( {x - 3} \right)}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{3x - 2}{4}$$</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.55">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{\frac{3x^{2} + 7x + 2}{4x + 24}}{\frac{3x^{2} - 14x - 5}{x^{2} + x - 30}}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.56">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{\frac{y^{2} - 36}{2y^{2} + 11y - 6}}{\frac{2y^{2} - 2y - 60}{8y - 4}}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <p>If we have more than two rational expressions to work with, we still follow the same procedure. The first step will be to rewrite any division as multiplication by the reciprocal. Then we factor and multiply.</p>
    <example number="8.29">
      <problem>
        <p>Divide: $$\frac{3x - 6}{4x - 4} \cdot \frac{x^{2} + 2x - 3}{x^{2} - 3x - 10} \div \frac{2x + 12}{8x + 16}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite the division as multiplication
by the reciprocal.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the numerators and the denominators,
and then multiply.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify by dividing out common factors.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.57">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{4m + 4}{3m - 15} \cdot \frac{m^{2} - 3m - 10}{m^{2} - 4m - 32} \div \frac{12m - 36}{6m - 48}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="8.58">
      <p>Divide: $$\frac{2n^{2} + 10n}{n - 1} \div \frac{n^{2} + 10n + 24}{n^{2} + 8n - 9} \cdot \frac{n + 4}{8n^{2} + 12n}.$$</p>
